outside, not in front of a screen. Don't take my word for it, the code is
linked at the bottom of this page.
[/code]

[h2]What it is[/h2]
ZeD-GUI, the ZeroDay Graphical User Interface, is a complete interface for Project Zomboid Build 42: it replaces the inventory, the character and loot windows, the HUD and the menus, for controller or mouse and keyboard. In the fiction it runs on ZNIX, a made-up kernel built by a paranoid doomsday prepper. The look is inspired by Macintosh System 6 and 7, as well as DOS and the Texas Instruments TI-99/4A. This is not an endorsement of Apple, Microsoft, Texas Instruments or any other brand, unless you want to send Hermit some free stuff, and then this is totally an endorsement.

The pictures above are the manual: a 1993 programming book with my notes in the margins, one feature to a spread. The short version:
[list]
[*][b]Character and World windows[/b] for everything you carry and everything around you, with a card for every item.
[*][b]A HUD on a belt:[/b] your hands, your watch, a dashboard when you drive, and moodles where you want them.
[*][b]A main menu that is a desk,[/b] and a Mods screen that catches missing requirements and conflicts and shows on and off at a glance.
[*][b]A survival guide on F1,[/b] a 1987 manual or a plain window: the game's topics plus ZeD's own chapters, your keys or your controller's buttons, and the game's rules in numbers. The game's topics and rules are plugged into the game itself: when an update adjusts, adds or changes something, the book changes with it, as soon as the game does, matched to your version and your world's settings. F1 just became your new Alt-Tab.
[*][b]Hints and notes:[/b] a hint strip with the key for what you face, the game's overhead notes in a readable bubble and kept in Messages, and pins on the title bar.
[*][b]Controller support,[/b] with the buttons drawn for Xbox, PlayStation, Steam Deck or Nintendo, and a controller map in the quick wheel. The wheels have a toggle mode that needs no held input and no stick.
[*][b]Multiplayer in ZeD's own cards:[/b] tickets, the Admin tab, safehouses, factions and the Log.
[*][b]A Vehicle tab and a Cooking tab[/b] laid out like Crafting: a car's parts beside its diagram, and the game's pot-and-pan dishes built from a list and saved to make again.
[*][b]Full or simple:[/b] the belt, the watch, the dashboard, the radios and the machines come drawn as the real thing, or as plain cards with the same buttons.
[*][b]Your look:[/b] dark, light or high contrast, nine accent colors, two text sizes and see-through windows.
[/list]

[h2]Before you subscribe[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only[/b] (tested on 42.21 and 42.22), not Build 41. Tested at 4K, 1080p, the Steam Deck's 1280x800 and 1280x720.
[*][b]Use a new game or a copy of a save.[/b]
[*][b]It replaces the game's inventory and character windows,[/b] so buttons that other mods add to those windows don't show. Mods that use the game's own systems (context menu options, container buttons, items, recipes) work.
[*][b]It adds one item,[/b] a steel digital watch in the loot. Remove ZeD-GUI from a save and those watches go too; everything else can be added or removed at any time.
[*][b]It comes with a helper mod, ZeD picks,[/b] which stays empty until you pick files in Mods.
[*][b]Text is in English,[/b] with machine drafts in every other language the game has (see Known issues) and the game's own words wherever it has them.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, then turn on [b]ZeD-GUI[/b] in the main menu's Mods, after any other interface mods in the load order.
[*]Quit and start the game again. ZeD-GUI loads its fonts at start.
[*]Set the look and the HUD in Options, ZeD setup.
[/olist]
The inventory key opens the Character window, the loot key the World window.

[h2]Reporting a problem[/h2]
Post in the pinned [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion, with:
[list]
[*][b]the bug report:[/b] open the ZeD wheel and pick [b]Bug report[/b]. It copies every error with ZeD-GUI's version, your game version and your mod list, ready to paste;
[*]what you did, what you expected and what happened, with a screenshot if you can.
[/list]
[b]Safe mode:[/b] if ZeD-GUI stops you from playing, turn on Safe mode in Options, ZeD setup. The game's own screens come back. Safe mode can also hand back one screen at a time.

[h2]Server admins[/h2]
Mod ID: ZeD_UI. Every player needs it, because it adds an item. It runs on the server too, official Lua only. Its server extras are all off by default.

